{
  // A Worker script answers /api/* and the static assets serve everything else.
  // See docs/adr/0006-landing-page-and-app-paths.md (which path is which) and
  // docs/adr/0007-optional-backend.md (why there is a server at all).
  //
  // `main` was absent until Phase E ticket 04, and the comment that used to sit
  // here said so ("no Worker script and no `main`"). It is corrected rather than
  // left as a stale invariant: this config now ships a script, and a reader who
  // trusted the old sentence would conclude /api/* is unanswered.
  //
  // `assets.run_worker_first` is NOT optional, and that is the whole reason it is
  // here. `compatibility_date` is 2026-09-14, past the 2025-04-01 threshold where
  // a navigation request does not invoke the Worker script even when the path
  // matches. Without this, `fetch("/api/session")` from the app reaches the
  // Worker while a browser navigating to /api/session is served the assets
  // fallback — a half-failure that looks like the API being flaky. Scoped to
  // /api/*, so every other path keeps the assets' own behaviour.
  //
  // `not_found_handling` MUST NOT be "single-page-application": that value would
  // serve dist/index.html — the Landing Page — for every unmatched path, including
  // under /app/. `404-page` serves public/404.html instead.
  //
  // `html_handling` is deliberately unset: the default `auto-trailing-slash` already
  // serves /app (307 to /app/) from dist/app/index.html, redirecting the two to the
  // canonical spec form.
  //
  // `comp3tive` is the LIVE Worker's real name, not a placeholder. The deployed
  // origin is https://comp3tive.dimasawardhana.workers.dev/, and the name is the
  // first label of that host: a workers.dev URL is always `<worker>.<account>`.
  // Recorded 2026-10-13, verified by `curl` rather than by reading this file
  // back — see docs/ROADMAP.md, gate 3. Deploying this config updates that
  // Worker; it does not create a second one.
  //
  // The workers.dev host is the DEVELOPMENT origin, not the canonical one, and
  // that distinction is load-bearing rather than cosmetic. A workers.dev host
  // sits on the Public Suffix List's private section, so a credential registered
  // against it can never be shared with a custom domain (docs/adr/0008). Phase E
  // is built and tested here, where passkeys are disposable; the custom domain is
  // settled before real organizers can register, which is the moment a credential
  // stops being test data. Do not read this file's presence of a working origin
  // as the origin decision being closed.
  //
  // The D1 binding is the store (docs/adr/0007): one row per (account, community)
  // plus a version integer, because a conditional `UPDATE ... WHERE version = ?`
  // against the primary is the compare-and-swap the versioned push needs and KV
  // and R2 cannot provide it.
  //
  // `comp3tive-db` is the database's real name and `database_id` is its real id,
  // created 2026-10-15. A database id is an identifier, not a secret: what stays
  // out of the repo is the Worker's runtime secrets, which go through
  // `wrangler secret` (and `.dev.vars` locally, which .gitignore covers). The
  // binding is `DB` — not wrangler's suggested `comp3tive_db` — since one
  // database needs no disambiguating prefix.
  //
  // Local development needs no account and no real id: `wrangler d1 execute
  // --local` runs against a placeholder `database_id`, so `npm run dev` and the
  // unit tests never touch Cloudflare.
  "name": "comp3tive",
  "main": "server/index.ts",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-09-14",
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./dist",
    "not_found_handling": "404-page",
    "run_worker_first": ["/api/*"]
  },
  "d1_databases": [
    {
      "binding": "DB",
      "database_name": "comp3tive-db",
      "database_id": "d73ee1c8-7089-4da6-8ca4-91f5626b1a3a"
    }
  ]
}
